    {
      "additions": 5,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/17144f68d899648a7fd78409614b1ab0724bba4f/python%2Fsglang%2Fsrt%2Fsampling%2Fwatermarking%2FREADME.md",
      "changes": 6,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/python%2Fsglang%2Fsrt%2Fsampling%2Fwatermarking%2FREADME.md?ref=17144f68d899648a7fd78409614b1ab0724bba4f",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "python/sglang/srt/sampling/watermarking/README.md",
      "patch": "@@ -106,7 +106,11 @@ The Triton selector and state kernels live in `sglang/kernels/ops/sampling/texts\n \n Default-on and enforce-all modes require a server key. A server key without either mode remains available only to requests that opt in.\n \n-Use a regular config file readable only by the server account for keys; inline JSON is visible in the process command line. Launch-command, server-info, and crash-payload rendering redacts key fields and the `--watermark-config` value. Request logs redact watermark keys only when `--enable-watermark` is set. Process command lines, client request bodies, and process or GPU core dumps remain separate secret-bearing surfaces.\n+Use a regular config file readable only by the server account for keys; inline JSON is visible in the process command line. Redaction differs by surface:\n+\n+- Launch-command and server-info rendering always redact key fields and the `--watermark-config` value.\n+- Request logs, request dumps, and crash payloads redact watermark keys only when `--enable-watermark` is set. With watermarking off no server key exists, so client-supplied `watermark` fields are kept as-is.\n+- Process command lines, client request bodies, and process or GPU core dumps are not redacted and remain secret-bearing.\n \n ## Per-request control\n ",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/17144f68d899648a7fd78409614b1ab0724bba4f/python%2Fsglang%2Fsrt%2Fsampling%2Fwatermarking%2FREADME.md",
